{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112516-reporting-posts-culture","id":112516,"title":"Reporting Posts Culture","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-14T03:22:00-07:00","id":112516,"title":"Reporting Posts Culture","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> One thing I've noticed in my time on the internet is that I have <b>never</b> once used an ignore or report (or friend list etc.) function on a forum. White Wolf, here, RPGnet, AEG, Dumpshock.<br /> <br /> Partially I guess it's because I have a higher threshold for being offended but it's also that I just have no idea what the community at large would consider a 'reportable' post.<br /> <br /> Could anyone weigh in with opinions and preferably examples (fabricated ones if necessary to avoid upsetting others) of what you consider a 'reportable' post?<br /> <br /> When does a post switch from 'heated debate' to 'reportable'?<br /> <br /> Should you report a post that's not aimed at you? I.e.: two people are having a heated debate and you think one side has gone too far in what they're saying, should you report?<br /> <br /> Should you report a post that <b>is</b> aimed at you, you know that posts like that have been 'reportable' or 'bannable' or 'mod warning' or whatever before but it doesn't upset or offend you?<br /> <br /> E.g.: on RPGnet during the 'Sex/Rape Charms Exalted 3e previews' period I was accused in no uncertain terms of being a rape apologist because I expressed an opinion that I did not mind having charms like that in the game, I felt it expressed a nasty world in which people really did do these things. I know that poster was reported and was subsequently reprimanded for that. But I personally didn't report it nor did I feel the punishment was particularly warranted.<br /> <br /> Should I have reported? Should I be actively curating other people's posts because even if I am not offended others might be if they were subject to the same kind of post?<br /> <br /> Help me out here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T05:15:22-07:00","id":112552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112516-reporting-posts-culture#post112516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112516-reporting-posts-culture#post112516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When does a post switch from 'heated debate' to 'reportable?'</div> </div> </div> </div>When its contents break the terms of use for the site you're on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112516-reporting-posts-culture#post112516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should you report a post that's not aimed at you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Should you only report a crime you're a victim of, and be silent about ones you witness that only victimize other people?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112516-reporting-posts-culture#post112516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should you report a post that <b>is</b> aimed at you, you know that posts like that have been 'reportable' or 'bannable' or 'mod warning' or whatever before but it doesn't upset or offend you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what your question is, here. Are you asking if it's only okay to report a post in a fit of anger?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112516-reporting-posts-culture#post112516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should I have reported?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the dude got smacked down, then I'm guessing what he said violated the terms of use for RPG.net, so yeah, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T06:59:40-07:00","id":112605,"title":"","content":"Ditto what Jim said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T07:56:38-07:00","id":112638,"title":"","content":"As someone that also usually finds themselves on the &quot;I could see the case, but I wouldn't necessarily mod them, so I don't report it,&quot; I've been growing into reporting more frequently.<br /> <br /> I think the key part to remember is that mods usually don't mind you reporting something they decide not to do anything (visible) about. Reporting a heated thread that hasn't crossed over into moderation needing flame war gives the mods a chance to watch the thread and step in before things get too bad rather than after things have gone to pot. Reporting something aimed at you instead of firing back in the thread (I don't advise doing both unless you're being really careful about trying to not engage in the person side of the person's post) can be a good way to avoid escalation (even if you're not trying to escalate).<br /> <br /> Basically, it helps me to stop looking at the flag/report/etc. button as an &quot;alarm&quot; you're sounding when everything is going wrong. Instead I look at it as a preventative measure. Like going to the doctor because something feels off, rather than waiting until you know you're really sick. Even if 9/10 times you flag something that wasn't really a big deal, as long as the mods see that you're flagging stuff that is reasonable to have flagged (aka you're not flagging one poster all the time for the most minor slight, or constantly flagging people that disagree with you, etc.), I think it is better than just waiting for the big explosions before you say something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T07:59:42-07:00","id":112641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112516-reporting-posts-culture?p=112605#post112605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ditto what Jim said.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, is this a reportable post then? It appears to be breaking rule 2 'Respect the conversation' as it's little more than a '+1' that exceeds the minimum character count.<br /> <br /> Do people routinely report things like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T09:14:40-07:00","id":112691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112516-reporting-posts-culture?p=112641#post112641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, is this a reportable post then? It appears to be breaking rule 2 'Respect the conversation' as it's little more than a '+1' that exceeds the minimum character count.<br /> <br /> Do people routinely report things like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>no. do we need to explain why not to report that as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T09:47:43-07:00","id":112713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112516-reporting-posts-culture?p=112641#post112641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, is this a reportable post then? It appears to be breaking rule 2 'Respect the conversation' as it's little more than a '+1' that exceeds the minimum character count.<br /> <br /> Do people routinely report things like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. Sure, it's terse, but it relates to the topic and it's not going to start any fights - so why report it?<br /> <br /> I think rule 2 is mostly about threadcrapping and other similarly snide or off-topic posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 04-14-2014, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T11:30:43-07:00","id":112801,"title":"","content":"So we don't report things we think might break certain rules if they aren't going to cause a 'fight'.<br /> <br /> What separates a 'heated' comment with an 'amusing' remark from something 'inflammatory' or likely to cause a 'fight'?<br /> <br /> It's the main thing I really don't get. I don't presume to judge if someone elses comment is going to upset/inflame/etc. other users as I am clearly terrible at judging the responses of others in text. From my point of view it's a forum post from someone I'm probably never going to meet. But, demonstrably, other people do find some posts 'inflammatory' where I see nothing.<br /> <br /> I dunno, I guess I'm just really bad at reading mood or flow of conversation in text form.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I see people apologising to one another for a comment, before either side has expressed any offence, and I am mystified by why someone would consider what they wrote as requiring an apology.<br /> <br /> Are there any kinds of signifiers in text I could look out for? Either in my own writing to avoid posting in such a way as to offend or in other posts to flag? Rhetorical techniques to avoid? There's the obvious stuff like logical fallacies but those are failures in structure rather than in delivery and I'd find it rather unfair to report someone for a strawman argument. It's not a crime to be <i>wrong on the internet</i> after all.<br /> <br /> I'm probably better off just leaving it to the mods, I presume they've been selected for an ability to read the flow better than I and know when and how to step in.<br /> <br /> But that's a nice skill to have and if there are some secret techniques for doing it then I'd like to know them...<br /> <br /> Oh and JimB, comparing a post on a forum thread to a crime seems...excessive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T11:42:47-07:00","id":112813,"title":"","content":"Don't worry about reporting too much. The mods evaluate each report themselves, and I oversee them. We'd rather see a fight brewing and do nothing than have something get out of hand before we're aware of it.<br /> <br /> That's not in redtext, but it's my official response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T12:22:41-07:00","id":112850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112516-reporting-posts-culture?p=112801#post112801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we don't report things we think might break certain rules if they aren't going to cause a 'fight.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait wait wait: who's &quot;we?&quot; Can we be clear on that before we proceed further with that line of thought?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112516-reporting-posts-culture?p=112801#post112801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What separates a 'heated' comment with an 'amusing' remark from something 'inflammatory' or likely to cause a 'fight?'</div> </div> </div> </div>Tone, intent, and the reader's perception of the speaker's tone and intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112516-reporting-posts-culture?p=112801#post112801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demonstrably, other people do find some posts 'inflammatory' where I see nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then don't report something if your conscience is not offended by what you see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112516-reporting-posts-culture?p=112801#post112801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any kinds of signifiers in text I could look out for?</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest hint is when someone would rather talk about the user he's talking to than that user's arguments. Other than that...wishing you no offense, but I don't know how to explain this stuff. It is too basic to me to be able to explain with any accuracy, like trying to explain in words how to pick up a fork with your hand. It's not something I have to think about or examine; it's just something I do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112516-reporting-posts-culture?p=112801#post112801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">JimB, comparing a post on a forum thread to a crime seems...excessive.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules of a forum are in place to protect the community from those who would engage in behaviors the community considers unacceptable. The laws of a state are in place to protect the community from those who would engage in behaviors the community considers unacceptable. It's a very one-for-one situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T12:34:34-07:00","id":112865,"title":"","content":"I recall reading a well-written flame a long time ago. Despite the aggressiveness towards the one written to, it was generally well-received. It was humorous, and it generated other humorous responses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T10:20:50-07:00","id":113408,"title":"","content":"I try to keep it simple. If it offends me, I report it. It's not like a flag from me automatically earns someone a ban or anything. If 50 of us report it, maybe it'll be looked at more carefully, but if it's just me......eh, probably not. That's how we get a consensus about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}